      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T08:31:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find it more error-prone to have this as a member, compared to the current code that generates it in QueryTask:\n - It\u0027s not clear what the threading model is for this\n - It\u0027s not clear when it needs to be updated; easy to forget to update it so error-prone\n \nIIUC you\u0027re trying to avoid access to the cache on the QueryTask thread, but you end up using this member on multiple threads @GuardedBy(\"lock\"), which is a bit error-prone.\n\nI think you could do something like:\n\n - Add this as an argument to QueryTask constructor\n - Instead of calling executor.schedule(new QueryTask(config)...) in QueryTask, use handler.postDelayed(handleSendQuery), where handleSendQuery will build the QueryTask (on the handler thread) and call executor.submit.\n \nThis should allow us to get rid of the lock, as otherwise it\u0027s still needed for requestTaskFuture.",
